<article class="env-lemma" id="0EPN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EPN">Lemma <span data-tag="0EPN">71.9.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $D \subset X$ be a closed subspace. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$D$ is an effective Cartier divisor, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$D \to Y$ is a flat morphism. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then for every morphism of schemes $g : Y' \to Y$ the pullback $(g')^{-1}D$ is an effective Cartier divisor on $X' = Y' \times _ Y X$ where $g' : X' \to X$ is the projection. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Lemma <a href="/tag/083C" data-tag="083C">71.6.2</a> the property of being an effective Cartier divisor is étale local. Thus this lemmma immediately reduces to the case of schemes which is Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/056Q" data-tag="056Q">31.19.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>